T2C Phantom is NOT open source. Not GPLv3. Not MIT.

This public repository contains the CLIENT (the daemon you run).
It is source-available so anyone can audit it and verify the
absence of a backdoor.

The SERVER / public-relay source is private, for security reasons:
poisoned nodes (Sybil attacks) and protection of the network
topology. Do not expect that code in this repository.

No permission is granted to copy, modify, distribute, fork or
commercially integrate T2C Phantom without written authorization
from Association TUTODECODE.

Contact: contact@tutodecode.org
